<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Konstanz</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Konstanz, in English Constance, is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-constance">Lake Constance</a> where the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> leaves the lake, on the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>. A late Roman fort, it became a bishopric around 600, heading the largest diocese of the German lands, and later a free imperial city. From 1414 to 1418 it hosted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-constance">Council of Constance</a>, which ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-schism">Western Schism</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/konstanz.jpg" alt="Konstanz" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: JoachimKohler-HB · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rheintorturm_in_Konstanz.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
